title: 'sc-tracing: keep all events when a state_traceBlock filter is empty'
doc:
  - audience:
      - Node Dev
      - Node Operator
    description: |
      The RPC documentation says that an empty filter does not remove events. But
      `state_traceBlock` removed each event that did not have the filtered field, also
      when the filter was empty. Because of this, traces did not show events such as
      `ClearPrefix` and `StorageRoot`.

      An empty key or method filter now keeps all events. Filters that are not empty
      work as before. When the filters are omitted, the node still removes all events.
crates:
  - name: sc-tracing
    bump: patch
